<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-IRISH 2,000 GUINEAS RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-IRISH 2,000 GUINEAS RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Irish 2,000 Guineas,</p>
<p>a group one race for three-year-old colts and fillies, run over</p>
<p>one mile (1.6 kms) at The Curragh on Sunday:</p>
<p> 1. Desert King   3-1 (ridden by Christy Roche)</p>
<p> 2. Verglas	33-1 (Willie Supple)</p>
<p> 3. Rolmanov     11-1 (Richard Hughes)</p>
<p>12 ran. Revoque was the 11-10 favourite.</p>
<p>Distances: Three lengths, two lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Michael Tabor, trained by Aidan O'Brien in</p>
<p>Ireland.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 112,700 Irish punts ($183,925)</p>
</text>
